// ARCH40 / ARCH53.7 = Architecture sections; ADR-004; SPEC = G010 Spec R1-R3.
//
// Reading rules (apply to every expectation):
//   - Keys, not UUIDs. The glue maps fixture keys to canonical UUIDs.
//   - Context notation: "<actor>@<org>" is an Organization-only TenantContext,
//     "<actor>@<org>/<group>" a selected-Group TenantContext, resolved in the
//     actor's own live request scope unless the Context text says otherwise.
//     "sql:<actor>@<org>[/<group>]" is the attested direct runtime SQL
//     connection with that TENANT-ORG / TENANT-GROUP shape (DBISO), without
//     application predicates. "none" is a context-free probe. "trusted" is an
//     accepted lifecycle writer (event) that commits before the next check.
//   - Code: the external *access.Error code, "ok" for success, "committed" for
//     an event, "" for an SQL read (then Table/Visible apply) or an observation.
//   - Visible: the exact set of fixture keys visible in that table. Only rows
//     the fixture defines (seeded, plus step-created rows that exist by then)
//     are compared. An empty, non-nil slice means no row.
//   - Effect fields left "" are not asserted by this expectation.
//     Row: object row state after the operation ("absent" = no row), or
//     "updated"/"unchanged" for a Group or profile row. Bytes: provider bytes at
//     the object's key. Provider: calls into the objectstore.Store boundary
//     (spy count), "zero" or "nonzero". URL: an HTTP GET of the signed URL,
//     "200" (exact bytes) or "non2xx". Tx: whether a storage/facade transaction
//     began. Backend/Settings: D2 pooled-backend expectations.
//   - Every denial (any code other than ok/committed, and every zero-row or
//     zero-affected SQL result) means: no mutation of owned database or byte
//     state and, for storage, zero provider calls (SPEC R3, AC2).
//   - Pair names the earlier allowed expectation that is the denial's paired
//     positive.
//
